      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name}\n\nThank you for your reply.\n\nThe issue has been resolved, but I have discovered a different behavior between UnityConstraint and VRCConstraint, so I would like to report it.\n\nThe cause of the problem with my avatar is as follows.↓\n\n（Please refer to the image for the location where the issue occurred.）\n\n① I added a ScaleConstraint to the \"アーマチュア\" and set it to the Head because the \"neck-gear\" object was interfering with the field of view.\n\nAt this point, in local play, the size of the \"neck-gear\" becomes 0.\n\n② However, the VRCParentConstraint applied to the \"neck-core,\" which is directly under the アーマチュア, did not seem to work well with an object that had a size of 0.\n\nBecause of this, my model started experiencing issues.\n\nAs a current workaround, I was able to avoid the issue by reducing the weight of the ScaleConstraint in the アーマチュア from 1 to 0.99, making the size slightly larger than 0.\n\nThese are the differences in behavior between UnityConstraints and VRCConstraints that I discovered.\n\nShould I report this as a bug?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
