      "value": "@{64f13b9656c5480964b1d080|full_name} I'm afraid I still can't find a difference between VRChat constraints and Unity constraints on this avatar based on your description. The scale constraint on アーマチュア gives consistent results between Unity and VRChat constraints, with a weight of 1 setting the transform's scale to almost 0 in both cases when the head bone is scaled down. The scales applied are consistent with your images when the head is at its normal scale. Can you please describe the effect this issue has on your avatar compared to what you would normally expect?\n\nAlternatively, instead of using a scale constraint, I would recommend using a VRCHeadChop component instead: https://creators.vrchat.com/avatars/avatar-dynamics/vrc-headchop\n\nIn your case, you could try adding a VRCHeadChop component anywhere you'd like on your avatar and then assigning アーマチュア as a target bone with the Scale Factor set to 0, then removing the scale constraint on アーマチュア. This should hide that transform from first person while still keeping it visible in mirrors and to other players. I can see the Transform sequence on this avatar animates the weight of the scale constraint - you should be able to achieve the same effect with VRCHeadChop by animating the scale factor to 1 when it should become visible in first person.\n\nScale constraining a bone to the avatar's head in order to hide it from first person is not officially supported behavior and may not be possible in the future.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
