  "details": "After the update, the ParentConstraint started to oscillate repeatedly.\n\nSince the update on August 17th (when VRCConstraint was implemented), the ParentConstraint I applied to my avatar has started oscillating.\n\n(The blueprint ID of the public avatar is avtr_493a933a-4055-47fa-8da3-0f7df2ba6c3a.)\n\nThis bug appears to be entirely local, and it seems that the oscillation is not visible to others.\n\nAdditionally, this bug does not occur during animations.\n\nThis is a bug that did not occur before the update, and from what I have investigated, there doesn't seem to be any issues with the animation files.\n\nFor example, the first keyframe of the animation that sets the ParentConstraint to its default state (the animation that plays normally) and the animation that modifies the ParentConstraint parameters (played from the expression menu) are exactly the same. However, this bug does not occur with the latter animation.\n\nThese issues are occurring for all users who use this avatar. For the reasons mentioned above, I have determined that this is a bug caused by the VRChat update and something that needs to be addressed.\n\nThis text was translated using a translation tool, so there may be some unnatural sentences.",
